{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792513010,"nonce":"ep6E+rJCV6VtXMs9Kn6aIrx9yRk=","message":"Implemented extension-owned stdio LSP sessions and made Rayzor the built-in default Haxe language server, following the user's final transport/default decisions. TCP is outside the final scope; the transport comparison is recorded in 5d8fb52140867d25d48114b0b5f4b291aa015b3578adadb4a6d59b1364951534.\n\nRayScript exposes rayde.languages.registerServer/unregisterServer/servers with a languages.register capability. Registration owns a workspace process independently of tab/editor lifetimes. A script event-fiber failure preserves it; extension stop/disable/reload/capability revocation releases it. The default extension is enabled on startup but starts Rayzor lazily on the first Haxe document, preserving the process after all documents close. Settings expose executable, build file, standard library and macro budget; status notifies/logs and restart explicitly replaces the owned process. Uses the exact website/logo.svg from sibling Rayzor with its license.\n\nNative Rust workers handle process launch, one framed writer, stdout reader, stderr draining and asynchronous reaping, exchanging owned bytes across the HashLink ABI. UTF-8 Content-Length framing, UTF-16 positions, bounded input/output queues and frames, initialization/capabilities, full/incremental sync, document versions, cancellation, request timeouts, graceful shutdown, bounded restart/backoff and unsaved-buffer replay are covered. Request errors/timeouts keep the server alive. Completion, hover, signature help, definitions, diagnostics and Outline route to the registered provider, with the Haxe display fallback on disable/restart-limit exhaustion. Unsupported snippets/replacement forms and the initial capability limits are documented.\n\nExecutable discovery uses explicit settings, RAYZOR_LSP, packaged Rayzor, PATH and sibling release/debug builds. Staging copies an existing server and standard library without invoking a Rayzor Cargo build. Current development artifact uses system LLVM; release portability requirements are recorded in contributing/building.md.\n\nConcurrency audit of Rayzor 9492ccd5d7591c456fa3ca383379e8a0103eff31: independent protocol reader/writer threads and one session analysis thread, coalescing queued edits before compiling and answering requests sequentially. Multiple client requests may be in flight; analysis is not parallel within the session. Request/compiler unwinds are caught and macros have a budget. Cancellation currently does not interrupt a running analysis. No Rayzor source changes were needed; its existing unrelated working-tree files were preserved.\n\nValidation completed:\n- Built current Rayzor in its own existing target with its project configuration: cargo build --release --locked -p rayzor.\n- Rayzor current session suite: cargo test --release --locked -p rayzor-lsp --features compiler/llvm-dynamic --test session -- --test-threads=1: 9/9 passed, including failing macro recovery and subsequent valid requests.\n- RayDE scripts/check.sh passed with RAYDE_RAYZOR_LSP pointing at current Rayzor; 32 requests were in flight together and every hover returned the expected semantic declaration. Document close and unsupported request preserved the connection.\n- Focused LspChecks with RAYDE_RAYZOR_LSP=rayzor resolved the staged bin/rayzor automatically and passed semantic requests without an explicit standard library path. Fixture checks cover out-of-order replies, stale/cancelled responses, timeouts, incremental UTF-16 ranges, old diagnostic versions, same PID after closing all documents, crash replay, restart limits, startup laziness, capability denial/revocation, status/restart and RayScript event-fiber exceptions.\n- Native rayde-rayscript suite: 14/14 tests passed, including partial/malformed/oversized frames.\n- SNAPSHOT_ONLY=lsp passed both schemes with the real built-in manifest/script: completion acceptance, asynchronous hover/signature help, definition navigation, Outline, tab close/reopen persistence, default built-in discovery, and Settings fields/logo. Previews inspected under bin/lsp-snapshots.\n- Native bin/rayde and bin/RayDE.app rebuilt. Packaged/staged Rayzor binaries and logo match their source artifacts; packaged standard library is present. git diff --check and bash syntax check passed.\n\nLogs: bin/lsp-checks.log, bin/lsp-default-server-checks.log, bin/lsp-native-tests.log, bin/lsp-snapshots.log, bin/rayzor-current-build.log, bin/rayzor-lsp-session-tests.log, bin/lsp-app-build.log, bin/lsp-package.log. All native builds used the existing sibling targets; no worktree or extra target directory was created.","files":null}]}